<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">TokenTiming: A Dynamic Alignment Method for Universal Speculative Decoding Model Pairs</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Sibo XIAO
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>The State Key Laboratory of Blockchain and Data Security, Zhejiang University
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>College of Computer Science and Technology
<span id="id1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Correspondence:</span> sibodotxiao@gmail.com, {3220100587, xiezl, should}@zju.edu.cn

</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Jinyuan FU
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>College of Computer Science and Technology
<span id="id2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Correspondence:</span> sibodotxiao@gmail.com, {3220100587, xiezl, should}@zju.edu.cn

</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Zhongle XIE
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>The State Key Laboratory of Blockchain and Data Security, Zhejiang University
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Lidan SHOU
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>The State Key Laboratory of Blockchain and Data Security, Zhejiang University
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Accelerating the inference of large language models (LLMs) has been a critical challenge in generative AI. Speculative decoding (SD) substantially improves LLM inference efficiency. However, its utility is limited by a fundamental constraint: the draft and target models must share the same vocabulary, thus limiting the herd of available draft models and often necessitating the training of a new model from scratch. Inspired by Dynamic Time Warping (DTW), a classic algorithm for aligning time series, we propose the algorithm TokenTiming for universal speculative decoding. It operates by re-encoding the draft token sequence to get a new target token sequence, and then uses DTW to build a mapping to transfer the probability distributions for speculative sampling. Benefiting from this, our method accommodates mismatched vocabularies and works with any off-the-shelf models without retraining and modification.
We conduct comprehensive experiments on various tasks, demonstrating 1.57x speedup. This work enables a universal approach for draft model selection, making SD a more versatile and practical tool for LLM acceleration<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
          
          
          
          
          
          
          
        Our codes are accessible at <a href="https://github.com/SeabirdShore/TokenTiming" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">link</a></span></span></span>.</p>
  
</div>
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para ltx_align_bottom">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center" style="width:345.0pt;"><span id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"></span></p>
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<figure id="S1.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15545v1/../img/overview.png" id="S1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/206;" width="476" height="206" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Comparison of core points of TokenTiming with previous work. Previous methods (TLI) carries the transfer of probability distribution in the vocabulary space of <math id="S1.F1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{d}\cap\mathcal{V}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{d}\cap\mathcal{V}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. If the draft tokens fall outside the intersection, they will be accepted unconditionally, which violates the integrity of losslessness. TokenTiming constructs intact token mapping via DTW, ensuring lossless speculative sampling. </figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Speculative decoding (SD) accelerates LLM inference using a small draft model to propose tokens that are then verified by the larger target model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Leviathan et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.
The effectiveness of SD depends on a draft model that is both fast and accurate in approximating the target distribution <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Timor et al., 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. However, a fundamental assumption in current verification methods—the requirement of a shared vocabulary between the draft model and target model—
prevents the widespread adoption of SD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Miao et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sun et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. This single constraint leads to two significant practical barriers:</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_font_italic ltx_title_paragraph">Limited Selection of Draft Models.</h5>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SD requires that the target and draft models share the same vocabulary. Many target models are deployed independently, possessing unique vocabularies that fundamentally preclude the choice of draft models. On the other hand, even within the same model family (e.g., GPT-OSS-120B/20B) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI, 2025</a>)</cite>, the smallest variants often remain too large to provide a substantial draft acceleration. An effective draft model must possess a parameter scale significantly smaller than the target model to ensure high inference efficiency. This dual, stringent constraint on both scale and vocabulary compatibility makes finding the optimal draft model a major practical hurdle.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_font_italic ltx_title_paragraph">Costly and Inflexible Training.</h5>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a selected target model, obtaining a draft model with complete word alignment usually requires starting from the pre/post-training stage, e.g. Medusa <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cai et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, Eagle <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>. Furthermore, if switched to a new target model, the previously trained model will no longer align. This is extremely inflexible in the current era where there are numerous model types and model iterations occur rapidly.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To address this, several alignment algorithms for universal speculative decoding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Timor et al., 2025a</a>)</cite> have been proposed. These methods resolve the heterogeneity of model vocabularies by operating at the linguistic level. SLEM (String-level Exact Match) cannot perform probabilistic sampling, while the performance of TLI (Token-level Intersection) is constrained by the size of the vocabulary intersection between the draft and target models. In conclusion, these methods have only partially alleviated the problem, but they cannot fully meet all the requirements for implementing lossless speculative decoding.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To overcome these challenges, we present <span id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TokenTiming</span>, a novel universal speculative decoding framework that enables lossless acceleration across heterogeneous vocabularies. At the core of TokenTiming is <span id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dynamic Token Warping (DTW)</span>, a lightweight alignment mechanism inspired by Dynamic Time Warping <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sakoe and Chiba, 1978</a>)</cite> from time series analysis. Given a sequence of draft tokens, TokenTiming first converts it into a string and then re-tokenizes it using the target tokenizer to obtain a proxy token sequence. DTW is then applied to construct a many-to-many alignment between the draft and proxy sequences, enabling accurate transfer of probability distributions from the draft vocabulary to the target vocabulary. This alignment is performed <span id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">on-the-fly</span> during each decoding step, without requiring any retraining or model modification.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Our Contributions:</span></p>
<ul id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Universal Compatibility Without Shared Vocabularies:</span> TokenTiming allows any off-the-shelf draft model to be plugged in without strict vocabulary match.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Strong Empirical Performance Across Tasks:</span> On summarization, translation, code and math, TokenTiming attains up to 1.57× speedup over autoregressive baselines and surpasses universal SD rivals.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Approaching Homogeneous-Vocabulary SD SOTA Performance:</span> On 7B/33B Models, TokenTiming yields 2.27× speedup, closing in on Medusa and EAGLE-1/2 while retaining model flexibility.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15545v1/method.png" id="S1.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/140;" width="476" height="140" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span><span id="S1.F2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase illustrations of TokenTiming. (a)</span> illustrates the re-tokenization of Draft Tokens into Proxy Target Tokens, which are used to construct the mapping in the DTW. <span id="S1.F2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(b)</span> DTW calculation process (token distance matrix) and aligned token mapping <math id="S1.F2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}=[(S,Scale),(cal,Scale),(ing,ing),(Law,L),(Law,aw)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}=[(S,Scale),(cal,Scale),(ing,ing),(Law,L),(Law,aw)]</annotation></semantics></math>. The calculation rules for this mapping are presented in Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.1 Methodological Core ‣ 4 Method ‣ TokenTiming: A Dynamic Alignment Method for Universal Speculative Decoding Model Pairs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. <span id="S1.F2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(c)</span> Probability distribution of draft tokens is transferred based on the mapping <math id="S1.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="S1.F2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(d)</span> Dynamic alignment in every Draft-Verify iteration of Speculative Decoding.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Related Works</h2>

<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SD with Homogeneous Vocabularies</h5>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Speculative Decoding (SD) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Leviathan et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2023</a>)</cite> reduces inference latency by using a fast draft model to propose tokens that are then verified in parallel by a larger target model. There are many different types of speculative decoding approaches. Draft-head methods like Medusa <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cai et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, Hydra <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ankner et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and EAGLE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2025</a>)</cite> integrate auxiliary heads into the target model to propose sequences. In contrast, Jacobi-based approaches such as Lookahead Decoding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fu et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and CLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kou et al., 2024</a>)</cite> enable parallel n-gram generation without draft models. System-level efforts <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Miao et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024</a>)</cite> further optimize SD’s runtime efficiency in serving systems.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SD with Pruned Vocabularies</h5>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2025)</a></cite> proposed a vocabulary pruning strategy to enhance the efficiency of speculative decoding draft models. The core rationale is the pronounced long-tailed structure of token frequency distributions. An empirical analysis of Llama-3-8B on the SlimPajama dataset confirms this, showing that a vast majority of the vocabulary (75%) accounts for a small fraction (less than 5%) of token occurrences <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grattafiori et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Soboleva et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. The proposed method operates by calculating token frequencies on a dataset S and constructing a reduced vocabulary comprising only the most frequent tokens.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SD with Heterogeneous Vocabularies</h5>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Token-Level Intersection (TLI) for heterogeneous draft models, has been recently introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Timor et al. (2025a)</a></cite>, which normalizes the intersected distribution by zeroing out all out-of-vocabulary mass. Alternatively, Redistributing draft model Kernels (RDK) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Timor et al., 2025c</a>)</cite> uses a row-stochastic matrix <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> to convert the draft distribution <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> to a new distribution <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> via the operation <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}=M^{T}d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}=M^{T}d</annotation></semantics></math>. The resulting distribution <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and the target distribution <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> are then used for native speculative sampling.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Preliminaries</h2>

<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Speculative Decoding (SD)</h5>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the vocabularies of draft model <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and target model <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively.
SD accelerates autoregressive generation by letting <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> propose <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> tokens <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{D}=(d_{1},\dots,d_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐃</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{D}=(d_{1},\dots,d_{K})</annotation></semantics></math> in one shot;
<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> then verifies them in a <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">single</em> forward pass and rolls back at the first rejection.
The expected speed-up is <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\gamma+1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\gamma+1]</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in[0,K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in[0,K]</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of accepted tokens.
Crucially, standard verification assumes <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{d}=\mathcal{V}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{d}=\mathcal{V}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> so that each draft token <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be directly verified by <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Standard Speculative Sampling</h5>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Speculative sampling enables <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">lossless</span> acceleration by verifying multiple tokens in parallel.
Let <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the probability assigned by the draft model to token <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(t)</annotation></semantics></math> the corresponding probability under the target model.
A proposed token <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is accepted with probability <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\!\Bigl(1,\;\frac{q(t)}{p(t)}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\!\Bigl(1,\;\frac{q(t)}{p(t)}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>,otherwise it is rejected and a new token is sampled from the adjusted target distribution.
This acceptance rule guarantees that the final output distribution remains identical to the target model’s distribution.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Vocabulary Mismatch</h5>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{d}\neq\mathcal{V}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{d}\neq\mathcal{V}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
              
            Appendix <a href="#A11.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Appendix K Model Vocabulary Statistics ‣ TokenTiming: A Dynamic Alignment Method for Universal Speculative Decoding Model Pairs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> demonstrates detailed statitics of Vocabulary Mismatch</span></span></span>, the draft token sequence <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐃</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{D}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot be directly interpreted by <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:
the same surface form may be tokenised differently (e.g. <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"Scaling"</span> <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> one token in <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> but <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"Scal"+"ing"</span> in <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>),
and normalisation rules make re-encoding non-invertible, so the proxy sequence <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐭</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can diverge sharply from <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐃</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, collapsing the accept rate.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Method</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To address the fundamental challenges of vocabulary mismatch in universal speculative decoding, we propose <span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TokenTiming</span>, a novel algorithm built upon our core integration of <span id="S4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dynamic Token Warping (DTW)</span>. The complete algorithmic procedure is formally presented in Fig. <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Costly and Inflexible Training. ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ TokenTiming: A Dynamic Alignment Method for Universal Speculative Decoding Model Pairs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Methodological Core</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dynamic Token Warping (DTW)</span> algorithm serves as the core alignment components in our framework, addressing the fundamental challenge of vocabulary mismatch between heterogeneous tokenizers. As formally presented in Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.1 Methodological Core ‣ 4 Method ‣ TokenTiming: A Dynamic Alignment Method for Universal Speculative Decoding Model Pairs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, DTW establishes an optimal many-to-many mapping between draft token sequence <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=(d_{1},\dots,d_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=(d_{1},\dots,d_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> and proxy target token sequence <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=(t_{1},\dots,t_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=(t_{1},\dots,t_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> through dynamic programming.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm operates by constructing a cumulative cost matrix <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathbb{R}^{k\times m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathbb{R}^{k\times m}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each entry <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the minimum cumulative distance to align the first <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> draft tokens with the first <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> target tokens. The local dissimilarity <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(x_{i},y_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(x_{i},y_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> between tokens is computed using an appropriate distance metric, with Levenshtein distance serving as our primary choice due to its effectiveness in capturing token-level edits.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure computational efficiency while maintaining alignment quality, we implement the <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sakoe-Chiba Band</span> constraint:
<math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=\{(i,j)\mid|i-j|\leq w\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=\{(i,j)\mid|i-j|\leq w\}</annotation></semantics></math>
This restriction limits the search space to a diagonal band of width <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, reducing computational complexity from <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(k\cdot m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(k\cdot m)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(w\cdot\max(k,m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(w\cdot\max(k,m))</annotation></semantics></math>. The window size <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is carefully selected to balance alignment accuracy and computational overhead, with the additional constraint that <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta id&lt;w\land\Delta id&lt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta id&lt;w\land\Delta id&lt;k</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta id" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta id</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the sequence order id deviation between matched tokens. The optimal alignment path <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}=[(i_{1},j_{1}),\dots,(i_{L},j_{L})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}=[(i_{1},j_{1}),\dots,(i_{L},j_{L})]</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained through backtracking from <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{k,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{k,m}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1,1}</annotation></semantics></math>, following the minimal cost path through the accumulated distance matrix. This path establishes the crucial correspondence that enables subsequent probability transfer between token sequences.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Dynamic Token Warpping (DTW)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Token sequences <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}=(x_{1},\dots,x_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}=(x_{1},\dots,x_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}=(y_{1},\dots,y_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}=(y_{1},\dots,y_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>,
edit distance metric <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, window size <math id="alg1.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Optimal path <math id="alg1.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and total cost <math id="alg1.l0a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             Initialize <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0..m,0..n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0..m,0..n}</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0,0}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0,0}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>;
<math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i,0},C_{0,j}\leftarrow\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i,0},C_{0,j}\leftarrow\infty</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\leftarrow\max(1,i-w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\leftarrow\max(1,i-w)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(n,i+w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(n,i+w)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i,j}\leftarrow d(x_{i},y_{j})+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i,j}\leftarrow d(x_{i},y_{j})+</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\quad\min\{C_{i-1,j},C_{i,j-1},C_{i-1,j-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\quad\min\{C_{i-1,j},C_{i,j-1},C_{i-1,j-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{C^{*}}\leftarrow C_{m,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐂</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{C^{*}}\leftarrow C_{m,n}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}\leftarrow[]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}\leftarrow[]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\leftarrow(m,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\leftarrow(m,n)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\neq(0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\neq(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
              Prepend <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)\leftarrow\underset{\begin{subarray}{c}(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})\in\{(i-1,j),(i,j-1),(i-1,j-1)\}\end{subarray}}{\mathrm{argmin}\&gt;C_{i^{\prime},j^{\prime}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>argmin</mi><mo lspace="0.220em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)\leftarrow\underset{\begin{subarray}{c}(i^{\prime},j^{\prime})\in\{(i-1,j),(i,j-1),(i-1,j-1)\}\end{subarray}}{\mathrm{argmin}\&gt;C_{i^{\prime},j^{\prime}}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Methodological Pipeline</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TokenTiming</span>, as formally presented in Alg. <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 4.2.3 Prefix Iteration ‣ 4.2 Methodological Pipeline ‣ 4 Method ‣ TokenTiming: A Dynamic Alignment Method for Universal Speculative Decoding Model Pairs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, integrates DTW alignment into a cohesive speculative decoding framework, enabling efficient cross-tokenizer acceleration while preserving output distribution losslessness.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.2.1 </span>Draft Token Conversion</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At each decoding iteration, the draft model <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> autoregressively generates token sequence <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=(d_{1},\dots,d_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=(d_{1},\dots,d_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> from the current prefix <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}</annotation></semantics></math>. To bridge the <span id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">heterogeneous tokenizer</span> gap, we employ a dual-conversion pipeline: <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is first encoded into an intermediate string representation <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Tokenizer}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Tokenizer</mtext><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Tokenizer}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, then decoded into the target vocabulary space using <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Tokenizer}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>Tokenizer</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Tokenizer}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to yield <span id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proxy Target Tokens</span> <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{T}=(t_{1},\dots,t_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐓</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{T}=(t_{1},\dots,t_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>. Notably, the cardinality mismatch <math id="S4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\neq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\neq k</annotation></semantics></math> frequently arises due to fundamental tokenizer disparities, necessitating our DTW alignment mechanism.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.2.2 </span>Verification via Speculative Sampling</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Leveraging the mapped probability distribution <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p(t_{j})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p(t_{j})\}</annotation></semantics></math> derived from DTW alignment, the target model <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> performs parallel verification through a single forward pass over the proposed sequence <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, computing the true conditional probabilities <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{q(t_{j})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{q(t_{j})\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Tokens are sequentially accepted according to the speculative decoding criterion:
<math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Accept }t_{j}\quad\text{if}\quad r&lt;\min\left(1,\frac{q(t_{j})}{p(t_{j})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Accept </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>if</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Accept }t_{j}\quad\text{if}\quad r&lt;\min\left(1,\frac{q(t_{j})}{p(t_{j})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\sim U(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\sim U(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. This mechanism guarantees that the output distribution exactly matches that of the target model, preserving generative quality while enabling acceleration. The verification process terminates at the first rejection instance, yielding <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> accepted tokens where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\gamma\leq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\gamma\leq m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.2.3 </span>Prefix Iteration</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Upon accepting <math id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> tokens <math id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{*}=(t_{1},\dots,t_{\gamma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{*}=(t_{1},\dots,t_{\gamma})</annotation></semantics></math>, the target model generates the subsequent token distribution <math id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{M_{t}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{P},t_{1},\dots,t_{\gamma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{M_{t}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{P},t_{1},\dots,t_{\gamma})</annotation></semantics></math>. We sample <math id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\gamma+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\gamma+1}</annotation></semantics></math> from this distribution and update the decoding prefix as <math id="S4.SS2.SSS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}\leftarrow\mathbf{P}\oplus(t_{1},\dots,t_{\gamma},t_{\gamma+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}\leftarrow\mathbf{P}\oplus(t_{1},\dots,t_{\gamma},t_{\gamma+1})</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes one decoding iteration, preparing the system for subsequent draft generation and verification cycles.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> TokenTiming</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
                
                
               Prefix <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, draft <math id="alg2.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, target <math id="alg2.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, length <math id="alg2.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
                
                
               Full sequence <math id="alg2.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
                
                
               <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\leftarrow\mathbf{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>𝐏</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\leftarrow\mathbf{P}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
                
                
               <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> last token of <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\neq\texttt{&lt;EOS&gt;}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>≠</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">&lt;EOS&gt;</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\neq\texttt{&lt;EOS&gt;}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\leftarrow M_{\text{d}}.\text{generate}(\mathbf{X},k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>d</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mtext>generate</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\leftarrow M_{\text{d}}.\text{generate}(\mathbf{X},k)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}\leftarrow\text{Tokenizer}_{d}.\text{encode}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mtext>Tokenizer</mtext><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mtext>encode</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}\leftarrow\text{Tokenizer}_{d}.\text{encode}(D)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\leftarrow\text{Tokenizer}_{t}.\text{decode}(\mathbf{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mtext>Tokenizer</mtext><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mtext>decode</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\leftarrow\text{Tokenizer}_{t}.\text{decode}(\mathbf{S})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}\leftarrow\text{DTW}(D,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>DTW</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}\leftarrow\text{DTW}(D,T)</annotation></semantics></math> {Core alignment}

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
                
                
                <span id="alg2.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|T|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|T|</annotation></semantics></math> in parallel <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
                
                
