<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Losslessness</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before proceeding to the core proof, we must formalize the process by which the draft probability distribution <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is generated. This process is critical for bridging the vocabularies of the draft and target models.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be the vocabularies for the draft and target models, respectively. The draft model, <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, generates a sequence of its native tokens, <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=(d_{1},\dots,d_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=(d_{1},\dots,d_{K})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}\in V_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}\in V_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, along with their corresponding probabilities. This output from the draft model is then transformed into distribution <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t)</annotation></semantics></math> over the target vocabulary <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> through a deterministic, two-stage procedure:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Re-tokenization:</span> A deterministic function, <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\text{retokenize}}:V_{d}^{*}\to V_{t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>retokenize</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\text{retokenize}}:V_{d}^{*}\to V_{t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, converts the sequence of draft tokens into a sequence of proxy target tokens. This function is a composition of the draft model’s decoding function (<math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{decode}}:V_{d}^{*}\to\Sigma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>decode</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{decode}}:V_{d}^{*}\to\Sigma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the string space) and the target model’s encoding function (<math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{encode}}:\Sigma^{*}\to V_{t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>encode</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{encode}}:\Sigma^{*}\to V_{t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>). This yields the proxy target sequence <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{T}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=(t_{1},\dots,t_{m})=F_{\text{retokenize}}(D)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mtext>retokenize</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=(t_{1},\dots,t_{m})=F_{\text{retokenize}}(D)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Probability Mapping:</span> An alignment, <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}=\text{DTW}(D,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>DTW</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}=\text{DTW}(D,T)</annotation></semantics></math>, is computed between the draft and proxy sequences. The proposal probability <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> for each token in the target sequence <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is then constructed based on the probabilities of the draft tokens <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{d_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{d_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> that are mapped to <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> by the alignment <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. This mapping ensures that the probabilistic information from the draft model is transferred to the target vocabulary space.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Crucially, this entire procedure constitutes a deterministic function that takes the raw output of the draft model and produces the draft distribution <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. The subsequent proof of losslessness is a property of the verification and correction mechanism. This mechanism is valid for <span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">any</span> such draft distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">With this understanding, we can proceed with the proof by decomposing the generation of the next token into two mutually exclusive paths.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Analysis of the Acceptance Path</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This path occurs if the draft mechanism proposes <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}=t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}=t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and this draft is accepted. The algorithm’s acceptance criterion is that a random number <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\sim U(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\sim U(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> must be less than the ratio <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\left(1,\frac{q(t^{*})}{p(t^{*})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\left(1,\frac{q(t^{*})}{p(t^{*})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. The probability of this path is therefore a joint probability:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(\text{Acceptance},\text{token}=t^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Acceptance</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>token</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(\text{Acceptance},\text{token}=t^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P(\text{propose }t_{1}=t^{*})\times P(\text{accept }t_{1}|t_{1}=t^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>propose </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>accept </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P(\text{propose }t_{1}=t^{*})\times P(\text{accept }t_{1}|t_{1}=t^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=p(t^{*})\cdot\min\left(1,\frac{q(t^{*})}{p(t^{*})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p(t^{*})\cdot\min\left(1,\frac{q(t^{*})}{p(t^{*})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By moving <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> inside the <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>min</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min</annotation></semantics></math> function, we can simplify this expression:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(\text{Acceptance},\text{token}=t^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Acceptance</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>token</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(\text{Acceptance},\text{token}=t^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min\left(p(t^{*})\cdot 1,p(t^{*})\cdot\frac{q(t^{*})}{p(t^{*})}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min\left(p(t^{*})\cdot 1,p(t^{*})\cdot\frac{q(t^{*})}{p(t^{*})}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\min(p(t^{*}),q(t^{*}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\min(p(t^{*}),q(t^{*}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Analysis of the Rejection Path</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This path occurs if the first proposed token <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> (which can be any token <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>) is rejected. Following this rejection, a correction token is sampled, and we are interested in the case where this token is <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. The probability is:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(\text{Rejection},\text{token}=t^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Rejection</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>token</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(\text{Rejection},\text{token}=t^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P(\text{reject }t_{1})\times P(\text{sample }t^{*}|\text{rejection})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>reject </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>sample </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mtext>rejection</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P(\text{reject }t_{1})\times P(\text{sample }t^{*}|\text{rejection})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We will calculate these two terms separately.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">1. Total Rejection Probability.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The total probability of rejecting the first draft, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(\text{reject }t_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>reject </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\text{reject }t_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>, is found by summing the rejection probabilities over all possible proposed tokens <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. A token <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is rejected if the acceptance criterion is not met.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(\text{reject }t_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>reject </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(\text{reject }t_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t^{\prime}}P(\text{propose }t_{1}=t^{\prime}\&amp;\text{ reject }t_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>propose </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">&amp;</mo><mrow><mtext> reject </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t^{\prime}}P(\text{propose }t_{1}=t^{\prime}\&amp;\text{ reject }t_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t^{\prime}}p(t^{\prime})\cdot\left(1-\min\left(1,\frac{q(t^{\prime})}{p(t^{\prime})}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t^{\prime}}p(t^{\prime})\cdot\left(1-\min\left(1,\frac{q(t^{\prime})}{p(t^{\prime})}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t^{\prime}}\left(p(t^{\prime})-\min(p(t^{\prime}),q(t^{\prime}))\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t^{\prime}}\left(p(t^{\prime})-\min(p(t^{\prime}),q(t^{\prime}))\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t^{\prime}}p(t^{\prime})-\sum_{t^{\prime}}\min(p(t^{\prime}),q(t^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t^{\prime}}p(t^{\prime})-\sum_{t^{\prime}}\min(p(t^{\prime}),q(t^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a probability distribution, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t^{\prime}}p(t^{\prime})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t^{\prime}}p(t^{\prime})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. We define the total acceptance probability as <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\sum_{t^{\prime}}\min(p(t^{\prime}),q(t^{\prime}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\sum_{t^{\prime}}\min(p(t^{\prime}),q(t^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the total rejection probability is:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(\text{reject }t_{1})=1-\beta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>reject </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\text{reject }t_{1})=1-\beta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">2. Adjusted Distribution Sampling.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The algorithm specifies that upon rejection of a proposed token, a correction step is performed. This step involves sampling a new token from the <span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">adjusted target distribution</span>, which we will call <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. This distribution is specifically constructed to account for the remaining probability mass. Its unnormalized form is the part of the target distribution not covered by the draft, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(0,q(t)-p(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(0,q(t)-p(t))</annotation></semantics></math>. The distribution is normalized by the total rejection probability, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q^{\prime}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q^{\prime}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\max(0,q(t)-p(t))}{\sum_{x}\max(0,q(x)-p(x))}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\max(0,q(t)-p(t))}{\sum_{x}\max(0,q(x)-p(x))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{q(t)-\min(q(t),p(t))}{1-\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{q(t)-\min(q(t),p(t))}{1-\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The probability of sampling <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> after a rejection is therefore <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}(t^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}(t^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">3. Final Rejection Path Probability.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Multiplying the total rejection probability by the conditional probability of sampling <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> gives:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(\text{Rejection},\text{token}=t^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Rejection</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>token</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(\text{Rejection},\text{token}=t^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P(\text{reject }t_{1})\times P(\text{sample }t^{*}|\text{rejection})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>reject </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>sample </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mtext>rejection</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P(\text{reject }t_{1})\times P(\text{sample }t^{*}|\text{rejection})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\beta)\cdot q^{\prime}(t^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\beta)\cdot q^{\prime}(t^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\beta)\cdot\frac{q(t^{*})-\min(q(t^{*}),p(t^{*}))}{1-\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\beta)\cdot\frac{q(t^{*})-\min(q(t^{*}),p(t^{*}))}{1-\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=q(t^{*})-\min(p(t^{*}),q(t^{*}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=q(t^{*})-\min(p(t^{*}),q(t^{*}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Combining the Paths</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The total probability of the next validated token being <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sum of the probabilities from the Acceptance and Rejection paths:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P(\text{next token}=t^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>next token</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P(\text{next token}=t^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=P(\text{Acceptance},t^{*})+P(\text{Rejection},t^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Acceptance</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Rejection</mtext><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=P(\text{Acceptance},t^{*})+P(\text{Rejection},t^{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\min(p(t^{*}),q(t^{*}))}_{\text{From Acceptance Path}}+\underbrace{\bigl(q(t^{*})-\min(p(t^{*}),q(t^{*}))\bigr)}_{\text{From Rejection Path}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>From Acceptance Path</mtext></munder><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>From Rejection Path</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\min(p(t^{*}),q(t^{*}))}_{\text{From Acceptance Path}}+\underbrace{\bigl(q(t^{*})-\min(p(t^{*}),q(t^{*}))\bigr)}_{\text{From Rejection Path}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(p(t^{*}),q(t^{*}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(p(t^{*}),q(t^{*}))</annotation></semantics></math> terms cancel each other out, yielding the final result:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P(\text{next token}=t^{*})=q(t^{*})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>next token</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐭</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P(\text{next token}=t^{*})=q(t^{*})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Example of Generated Text</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1055.44" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 1055.44" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1055.44) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#0000BF;" fill="#0000BF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 1049.53 C 0 1052.8 2.64 1055.44 5.91 1055.44 L 647.24 1055.44 C 650.51 1055.44 653.15 1052.8 653.15 1049.53 L 653.15 5.91 C 653.15 2.64 650.51 0 647.24 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2FF;" fill="#F2F2FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 1049.53 C 1.97 1051.71 3.73 1053.47 5.91 1053.47 L 647.24 1053.47 C 649.42 1053.47 651.18 1051.71 651.18 1049.53 L 651.18 5.91 C 651.18 3.73 649.42 1.97 647.24 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#0000BF;" fill-opacity="1.0" stroke="#0000BF" stroke-dasharray="2.84528pt,2.84528pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 1.97 967.74 L 651.18 967.74"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 982.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.07em;--ltx-fo-height:4.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="62.11" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 59.42)" width="609.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.07em;">
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Draft model: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-1.5B
<br class="ltx_break">Target model: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-70B
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Prefix: The field of Artificial Intelligence has seen tremendous growth in recent years. One of the most exciting areas of research is</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.07em;--ltx-fo-height:67.9em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="942.16" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 939.47)" width="609.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.07em;">
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The field of Artificial Intelligence has seen tremendous growth in recent years. One of the most exciting areas of research is Reinforcement Learning (RL), which involves training agents to make decisions in complex, uncertain environments. In this blog post, we will explore the concept of policy in reinforcement learning, its types, and the importance of policy optimization.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">### What is a Policy in Reinforcement Learning?</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In reinforcement learning, a **policy** is a strategy that an agent uses to decide actions based on the current state of the environment. It can be thought of as a function, often denoted as <math id="A2.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>(a|s), which takes the current state (s) and returns an action (a) or a probability distribution over possible actions. The goal of the agent is to learn an optimal policy that maximizes the cumulative reward over time.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">### Types of Policies</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Policies in RL can be categorized in different ways. Here are some common types:</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. **Deterministic Policy**:
- A deterministic policy always selects the same action for a given state. It is a direct mapping from states to actions. For example,<math id="A2.p1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>(s) = a.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. **Stochastic Policy**:
- A stochastic policy, on the other hand, selects actions probabilistically. It outputs a probability distribution over possible actions given a state. This is often useful in exploration-exploitation trade-offs, where the agent might sometimes choose a suboptimal action to discover better ones.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. **Parametric Policy**:
- Parametric policies are defined by a set of parameters. These parameters can be adjusted during training to improve the policy. Examples include neural networks, where the weights and biases are the parameters.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4. **Non-Parametric Policy**:
- Non-parametric policies do not rely on a fixed set of parameters. Instead, they might be represented by lookup tables or other structures that can grow with the data. These are less common in deep RL settings.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">### Policy Optimization</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Policy optimization is the process of adjusting the parameters of a policy to maximize the cumulative reward. The goal is to find the optimal policy <math id="A2.p1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>* that maximizes the expected total reward. There are several approaches to policy optimization, each with its strengths and weaknesses.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">#### 1. **Value-Based Methods**
- These methods focus on estimating the value function, which indicates the expected cumulative reward from a given state. The policy is then derived by selecting actions that maximize this value.
- Example: Q-Learning</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">#### 2. **Policy-Based Methods**
- These methods directly optimize the policy by adjusting its parameters to increase the cumulative reward. They often use gradient ascent to update the policy parameters.
- Example: REINFORCE</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">#### 3. **Actor-Critic Methods**
- These methods combine the benefits of value-based and policy-based approaches. They maintain both a policy (actor) and a value function (critic). The critic evaluates the actions taken by the actor, and the actor adjusts its policy based on the critic’s feedback.
- Example: A3C (Asynchronous Advantage Actor-Critic)</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">### Importance of Policy Optimization</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. **Maximizing Cumulative Reward**: The primary goal in RL is to maximize the cumulative reward. Policy optimization ensures that the agent learns a policy that achieves this.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. **Adaptability**: Through optimization, the policy can adapt to different environments and scenarios, making the agent more versatile.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. **Handling Complex Environments**: In complex and uncertain environments, a well-optimized policy allows the agent to make informed decisions even when the outcomes are not immediately clear.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.19.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4. **Efficiency**: Efficient policy optimization algorithms enable agents to learn quickly, which is crucial in real-world applications where training time is a constraint.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.20.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">### Common Policy Optimization Algorithms</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.21.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. **REINFORCE**: A basic policy gradient algorithm that updates the policy parameters by the gradient of the expected cumulative reward.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.22" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.22.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. **A2C (Advantage Actor-Critic)**: An extension of A3C that uses synchronous updates, making it more stable and efficient.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.23" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.23.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. **PPO (Proximal Policy Optimization)**: A popular algorithm that constrains the policy updates to be close to the previous policy, ensuring stable training.</span></span>
<span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.24" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.pic1.2.24.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4. **TRPO (Trust Region Policy Optimization)**: Similar to PPO but uses a more rigorous mathematical approach to constrain policy updates.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Details of Generation</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Candidate Length Strategy</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopted the candidate sequence length calculation strategy from the official implementation of Hugging Face Transformers. The rules are as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The calculation for the maximum number of new tokens, <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is constrained by both the system’s capacity and a role-specific limit. It is given by:</p>
<table id="A3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{\text{max}}=\min(|\mathbf{P}|,\text{Cfg}_{\text{max}}-L_{\text{cur}}-1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐏</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Cfg</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>cur</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{\text{max}}=\min(|\mathbf{P}|,\text{Cfg}_{\text{max}}-L_{\text{cur}}-1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The calculation for the minimum number of new tokens, <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{\text{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{\text{min}}</annotation></semantics></math>, ensures that the generation meets a minimum length requirement without exceeding the calculated maximum, while also being non-negative. It is given by:</p>
<table id="A3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{\text{min}}=\max\left(0,\min(\Delta L_{\text{max}},\text{Cfg}_{\text{min}}-L_{\text{cur}})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Cfg</mtext><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>cur</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{\text{min}}=\max\left(0,\min(\Delta L_{\text{max}},\text{Cfg}_{\text{min}}-L_{\text{cur}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The final number of candidate tokens for verification is:</p>
<table id="A3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=|(p_{D}&gt;=\alpha)\odot D|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>&gt;=</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=|(p_{D}&gt;=\alpha)\odot D|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L=\begin{cases}\Delta L_{\text{max}},&amp;\text{if }f&gt;\Delta L_{\text{max}}\\
f,&amp;\text{if }\Delta L_{\text{min}}\leq f\leq\Delta L_{\text{max}}\\
\Delta L_{\text{min}},&amp;\text{if }f&lt;\Delta L_{\text{min}}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L=\begin{cases}\Delta L_{\text{max}},&amp;\text{if }f&gt;\Delta L_{\text{max}}\\
f,&amp;\text{if }\Delta L_{\text{min}}\leq f\leq\Delta L_{\text{max}}\\
\Delta L_{\text{min}},&amp;\text{if }f&lt;\Delta L_{\text{min}}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where,</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{cur}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>cur</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{cur}}</annotation></semantics></math>: The current length of the input sequence.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Cfg}_{\text{max}},\text{Cfg}_{\text{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>Cfg</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext>Cfg</mtext><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Cfg}_{\text{max}},\text{Cfg}_{\text{min}}</annotation></semantics></math>: The absolute maximum and minimum sequence length permitted by the generation configuration.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathbf{P}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐏</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbf{P}|</annotation></semantics></math>: The number of tokens in the initial prefix sequence</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math>: The maximum number of <span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">new</span> tokens to be generated.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{\text{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{\text{min}}</annotation></semantics></math>: The minimum number of <span id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">new</span> tokens to be generated.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L</annotation></semantics></math>: final length for candidate sequence</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>: candidate tokens</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>: probability distribution of candidate tokens</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>: confidence parameters in generation configuration</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Number of Candidate Tokens per Iteration</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ C.2 Number of Candidate Tokens per Iteration ‣ Appendix C Details of Generation ‣ TokenTiming: A Dynamic Alignment Method for Universal Speculative Decoding Model Pairs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, we plot the number of candidate tokens and accepted tokens per iteration of the generation of examples in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Example of Generated Text ‣ TokenTiming: A Dynamic Alignment Method for Universal Speculative Decoding Model Pairs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> (<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Cfg}_{\text{max}}=20,\text{Cfg}_{\text{min}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Cfg</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Cfg</mtext><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Cfg}_{\text{max}}=20,\text{Cfg}_{\text{min}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>). The target model of the generation is DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-70B. and the draft model is DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-1.5B, which generates more than a thousand tokens within 53.8 seconds.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15545v1/../img/values_vs_iteration_spaced_plotv5.png" id="A3.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/289;" width="476" height="289" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Number of candidate tokens and accepted tokens per iteration of the generation of examples in Appendix B</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15545v1/../img/values_vs_iteration_spaced_plot_4tok.png" id="A3.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/289;" width="476" height="289" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Number of candidate tokens and accepted tokens per iteration with 4 candidate tokens per iteration of the generation examples</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15545v1/../img/values_vs_iteration_spaced_plot_8tok.png" id="A3.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/299;" width="476" height="299" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>Number of candidate tokens and accepted tokens per iteration with 8 candidate tokens per iteration of the generation examples</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
