<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span>Vocabulary intersection, union, and ratio statistics for common LLM model pairs.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section presents vocabulary statistics of all models in the experiment, including the independent vocabulary size of each model (Tab. <a href="#A11.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix K Model Vocabulary Statistics ‣ TokenTiming: A Dynamic Alignment Method for Universal Speculative Decoding Model Pairs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) and the vocabulary intersection, union, and intersection/union ratio of 20 model pairs (Tab. <a href="#A11.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Appendix K Model Vocabulary Statistics ‣ TokenTiming: A Dynamic Alignment Method for Universal Speculative Decoding Model Pairs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>). These statistics lay the foundation for subsequent verification of TokenTiming’s adaptability in heterogeneous vocabulary scenarios—by quantifying the degree of vocabulary overlap between different models, the performance verification boundaries of the algorithm in extreme low-intersection and high-intersection scenarios can be clearly defined.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A12" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix L </span>CPU/GPU Trace</h2>

<div id="A12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tokenization, Logic Operation, etc., these operations performed on the CPU may cause GPU synchronization, which will cause a significant performance degradation. In Figures <a href="#A12.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Appendix L CPU/GPU Trace ‣ TokenTiming: A Dynamic Alignment Method for Universal Speculative Decoding Model Pairs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>,<a href="#A12.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Appendix L CPU/GPU Trace ‣ TokenTiming: A Dynamic Alignment Method for Universal Speculative Decoding Model Pairs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>,<a href="#A12.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ Appendix L CPU/GPU Trace ‣ TokenTiming: A Dynamic Alignment Method for Universal Speculative Decoding Model Pairs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, we analyzed the CPU/GPU flow and confirmed that the introduction of DTW did not cause any performance bottlenecks. The blocking time introduced by TokenTiming in one decoding cycle is only 663 <math id="A12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu s</annotation></semantics></math>, which is insignificant compared to other parts.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A12.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15545v1/../img/cpuall.png" id="A12.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/221;" width="476" height="221" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>CPU stack trace visualization. The process segment for target logits calculation with DTW-related operations takes only 663<math id="A12.F10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu s</annotation></semantics></math>, highlighting its extremely short duration.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A12.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15545v1/../img/cpuamplify.png" id="A12.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/152;" width="476" height="152" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Enlarged view of the process segment for target logits calculation with DTW-related operations in the previous CPU trace figure.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A12.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.15545v1/../img/gpu.png" id="A12.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/34;" width="476" height="34" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>Visualization interface of GPU stream trace results, showing the time distribution of inference tasks under multiple threads and corresponding streams.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
